<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Stardew Tips handles hosting requests, emails, on-site search, and Google advertising data."><div class="simple-page container"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Last updated: 23 October 2026</p><p>This policy covers stardewtips.com, an independent guide site operated by Holly. Contact: <a href="mailto:holly125@yeah.net">holly125@yeah.net</a>.</p><h2>Reading and searching</h2><p>You can read the site without an account. This version has no login, comments, checkout, or newsletter form. The guide search runs in your browser; the search text is not submitted to a site search server. The current site code does not add a separate analytics tracker.</p><h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>The site is hosted through Cloudflare Pages. Requests necessarily share technical information such as your IP address, requested URL, browser information, and request time with the hosting infrastructure. This may be processed for delivery, reliability, security, and abuse prevention. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> for its processing practices.</p><h2>Google advertising and cookies</h2><p>Editorial pages include the Google AdSense script for the site’s publisher account. Script inclusion does not mean the site has been approved or that an ad will appear. Google and its partners may receive IP addresses, device or browser identifiers, and information about page visits, and may use cookies, web beacons, or similar technologies to deliver, measure, and personalize advertising, depending on consent and service configuration.</p><p>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on previous visits to this or other websites. Google’s advertising cookies enable it and its partners to serve ads based on those visits. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google’s advertising technologies</a>.</p><h2>Your advertising choices</h2><p>You can manage personalized advertising through <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">Google My Ad Center</a> and some participating vendors through <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/">YourAdChoices</a>. Your browser can block or delete cookies. These choices do not necessarily remove all advertising.</p><p>Where a consent message is presented, you can use its privacy controls to review or change your choices. Opt-out links are additional controls and do not replace consent where it is required.</p><h2>Email correspondence</h2><p>If you email us, we receive your address and the information you choose to include. We use it to respond, investigate corrections, or handle privacy requests. Do not send passwords or other sensitive account information. Correspondence is handled by our email provider; it is not published automatically.</p><h2>Retention and requests</h2><p>We keep correspondence as needed to handle the request and any follow-up. Hosting and advertising providers apply their own retention arrangements. Email us to request access to, correction of, or deletion of information you have supplied directly. We may need to verify a request and may retain information where legally necessary.</p><h2>External sites and children</h2><p>Linked websites have their own privacy practices. This site is intended for a general audience and does not knowingly solicit personal information from children under 13. A parent or guardian can contact us about information a child may have sent.</p><h2>Updates</h2><p>We will revise this page when the site’s data practices change and update the date above.</p></div></Base>
